1
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:15,000
[27 Years Ago, the Himalayas, India]

2
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:19,120
Take the picture.

3
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:25,420
All these human remains... Unbelievable.

4
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,820
I wonder what those Japanese are looking for.

5
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:35,310
Stay here, and they'll be cursed.

6
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:52,730
Doctor.

7
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:56,040
I found something very interesting.

8
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,620
See?

9
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,830
This is in very good condition.

10
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:04,350
And there is still muscle fiber that remains.

11
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:05,790
Yes.

12
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:29,650
[Funeral, Shiharu Nanase]

13
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:41,360
[Hall 1]

14
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:10,290
Sir? Sir, one moment.

15
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:12,050
Sir!

16
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:54,360
Haruka.

17
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,740
What are you doing?

18
00:02:56,740 --> 00:03:00,560
Who holds a funeral for their daughter,
when she's still alive?

19
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,550
I understand how you feel.

20
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:05,220
But you have to calm down.

21
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:09,380
Call off this ridiculous charade, now.

22
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:11,280
It's been four years.

23
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:12,870
We have to give her closure.

24
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:15,260
I saw Shiharu.

25
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:18,860
Let's talk outside.

26
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:21,030
Folks, please give us a moment.

27
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:23,910
Shiharu was there, at my thesis presentation!

28
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:29,720
It's not unusual to hold a funeral
for missing individuals.

29
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,070
But I saw her, after the flooding.

30
00:03:32,070 --> 00:03:35,800
And I'm telling you, you were seeing things.

31
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,010
No, I'm certain that was her.

32
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:42,810
DNA can then mutate,
or become an inverted repeat sequence.

33
00:03:42,810 --> 00:03:47,540
As DNA repeats,
it is more likely to undergo methylation.

34
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:00,380
A-Apologies.

35
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:04,430
DNA methylation affects
the transcription of genes,

36
00:04:04,430 --> 00:04:07,550
through a remodeling of the chromatin.

37
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:15,560
<i>I understand you can't accept it.</i>

38
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,360
But, Haruka.

39
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:21,070
You cannot sacrifice your future
for my daughter's sake.

40
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:25,000
Professor Ishimizaki sees the talent in you.

41
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,940
You have to move on.

42
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,500
Focus on your research.

43
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,850
Shiharu is alive.

44
00:04:33,670 --> 00:04:37,320
How can you assume otherwise?
You're her father.

45
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,810
Did you take your pills?

46
00:04:43,710 --> 00:04:45,090
Quit treating me like I'm sick.

47
00:04:45,090 --> 00:04:47,350
The clinic says you haven't visited.

48
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:51,250
Talking it out will help you process things.

49
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,920
Shiharu has passed on.

50
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:05,800
I apologize for the interruption.

51
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:08,680
Sir.

52
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:13,400
How much does he know?

53
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,720
Not a thing.

54
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,480
You're certain you can handle him?

55
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,430
Yes.

56
00:05:21,970 --> 00:05:29,770
[A mystery spanning two centuries]
[The whereabouts of his missing step-sister]

57
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:27,000
A monster?

58
00:06:28,810 --> 00:06:33,080
Yeah. It chased me into the mountains
when I was younger.

59
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:37,620
Which was just my excuse for getting lost.

60
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:39,800
Cute.

61
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,730
Didn't you ever make up stories like that?

62
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:46,750
Something to get your parents off your tail.

63
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:49,040
Maybe.

64
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,330
So, what about this monster?

65
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:57,700
Well, now I'm not so sure
if it really was an excuse.

66
00:06:57,700 --> 00:06:59,460
Oh?

67
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:03,190
It's not so uncommon

68
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:06,530
for kids to conflate their lies with reality.

69
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:08,670
So that's probably what's happening here.

70
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:11,270
"The basis for

71
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:14,870
all true understanding and knowledge
is the capacity to observe."

72
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:17,400
That's a quote from Barbara McClintock.

73
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,030
A famous geneticist.

74
00:07:19,030 --> 00:07:22,290
And here I thought
you were speaking wise words.

75
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:25,000
I just wanted to seem a bit smart.

76
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:29,120
Did you want to become a scientist?

77
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,830
I don't know.

78
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,060
It's coming down heavy.

79
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:36,120
- Let's hurry.
- Okay.

80
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:38,960
- Watch your steps.
- I will.

81
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:59,710
Professor Ishimizaki.

82
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:10,750
What a tough climb to make.

83
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:13,330
I hear this used to be an art museum?

84
00:09:13,330 --> 00:09:15,380
You followed me?

85
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:20,650
Your father was worried about you.

86
00:09:20,650 --> 00:09:22,570
Give him a call.

87
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,010
My "father", is it?

88
00:09:26,090 --> 00:09:28,780
It's been seven years since my mother passed.

89
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:31,620
My step-father is practically a stranger now.

90
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:37,410
Grateful as I am for his support.

91
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:43,980
I saw the state of her coffin.

92
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:48,460
I assume that was your doing?

93
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:55,020
You must think Shiharu is dead as well.

94
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:02,950
But I can't accept that.

95
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:09,400
You don't have to.

96
00:10:11,450 --> 00:10:14,110
There's no crime in believing she's alive.

97
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:18,210
But your belief in her,

98
00:10:19,210 --> 00:10:22,060
and assuaging your father's worries,

99
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:25,770
are things you can do simultaneously, no?

100
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:37,290
[Nichie Pharmaceutical Headquarters]

101
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:40,940
How much of our stock
does Xin Ming Ah own?

102
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,190
They've already purchased 20% of our shares.

103
00:10:43,190 --> 00:10:46,790
And they're about to acquire 10% more.

104
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:48,820
Can't we stop them?

105
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:51,520
They're a conglomerate from China.

106
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,640
It could lead to disastrous results.

107
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:56,160
What happens if we're bought out?

108
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:58,870
Can we keep "06-00" under wraps?

109
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:00,830
Barely any records remain

110
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:01,960
of such an old incident.

111
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:04,110
Check our archives again to be sure.

112
00:11:04,110 --> 00:11:07,660
We must eradicate any evidence of "06-00".

113
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:15,400
How is your daughter?

114
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,900
Mari?

115
00:11:18,590 --> 00:11:20,750
She's not doing well.

116
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:23,790
I can't even take her out in her wheelchair.

117
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:25,330
I see.

118
00:11:25,330 --> 00:11:26,580
When I met her before...

119
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:28,750
Haruka.

120
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:30,460
Yes, sir?

121
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:32,350
Can you do a job for me?

122
00:11:32,350 --> 00:11:33,830
What job?

123
00:11:33,830 --> 00:11:38,710
I want you to analyze
a skeleton we found in India.

124
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:40,900
Pardon?

125
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:43,580
Have you heard of Roopkund?

126
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:45,420
The lake up in the Himalayas.

127
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:48,250
Sounds familiar.

128
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:50,590
It's a cursed lake, I'll tell you that.

129
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:57,650
They've found about 800 human remains
from that area alone.

130
00:11:57,650 --> 00:11:59,160
800?

131
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,520
Was there a village nearby?

132
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:05,160
The lake is located
at an altitude of 5,000 meters.

133
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:07,710
That's no place
for a human village to thrive.

134
00:12:07,710 --> 00:12:14,260
<i>The bones themselves are attributed
to races all across Asia.</i>

135
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:16,580
<i>Their time of deaths don't match up either.</i>

136
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,710
<i>The 7th century, 10th century,</i>

137
00:12:18,710 --> 00:12:23,580
<i>and some even date to the 19th century.</i>

138
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:26,780
- <i>You participated in the excavations, sir?</i>
- <i>Indeed.</i>

139
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:32,410
Were these people making an offering?
Perhaps to a deity of sorts?

140
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:37,900
Even 27 years ago,
we never reached a conclusion.

141
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:40,100
Then why analyze a skeleton remain now?

142
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:45,660
Operations have resumed in India,
after they were cut short years back,

143
00:12:45,660 --> 00:12:48,120
due to a lack of funding.

144
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:53,510
My colleagues there
reached out for my assistance.

145
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:54,990
How many remains are we analyzing?

146
00:12:54,990 --> 00:12:56,330
Just one.

147
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:58,530
<i>Scientists in India
have deduced these remains</i>

148
00:12:58,530 --> 00:13:04,150
<i>are that of a young girl,
from over 200 years ago.</i>

149
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:05,980
So?

150
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:07,710
Are you up for the challenge?

151
00:13:07,710 --> 00:13:10,840
Yes, sir.

152
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:15,030
They say the lake is cursed.

153
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:17,840
According to the locals,

154
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:23,460
Roopkund afflicts any
who take its remains with them.

155
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:29,620
They say the remains themselves
are the skeletons of the damned.

156
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:33,540
Sounds like the perfect job for me.

157
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:40,030
Curses mean nothing

158
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,700
to a man who's lost everything.

159
00:13:45,870 --> 00:13:47,620
I see.

160
00:13:48,790 --> 00:13:51,680
You may think as such now.

161
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,170
But know this.

162
00:13:55,750 --> 00:14:01,260
The world you see now,
is not the whole truth.

163
00:14:12,490 --> 00:14:15,400
[Hyderabad, India]

164
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:44,480
Is there a god?

165
00:15:43,690 --> 00:15:46,100
You went to Roopkund.

166
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:48,950
Who told you...

167
00:15:58,830 --> 00:16:02,470
Say hello to the you of tomorrow.

168
00:16:04,370 --> 00:16:08,340
[Roopkund]

169
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:11,170
[Do you wish to delete this folder?]
[Yes]

170
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:12,490
[Deletion in progress]

171
00:16:19,210 --> 00:16:22,920
[I have acquired the remains.]

172
00:16:28,610 --> 00:16:31,720
[Send]

173
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:46,220
Everything will be okay.
Nothing to worry about.

174
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,090
You'll be okay.

175
00:19:08,550 --> 00:19:11,430
- Hello.
- Hey.

176
00:19:12,190 --> 00:19:14,370
Are those the bones from the lake?

177
00:19:14,370 --> 00:19:15,380
Yeah.

178
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:16,960
Need help with the analysis?

179
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:19,970
No, I finished up already.
Just waiting for the results.

180
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:23,440
These are from over 200 years ago?

181
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:27,290
Apparently. I'm having Itohara confirm it.

182
00:19:27,290 --> 00:19:29,480
Then I'll plug in the data for you.

183
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,860
Thanks.

184
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:32,550
Sure thing.

185
00:19:35,890 --> 00:19:37,940
- She's featured again.
- Who?

186
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:41,160
This woman. Is she that big of a deal?
[Kayoko Senba]

187
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:43,290
Kayoko Senba?

188
00:19:43,290 --> 00:19:45,210
Yeah, she's a genius.

189
00:19:45,210 --> 00:19:51,530
She's made advancements in neuroscience
most could only dream to achieve.

190
00:19:51,530 --> 00:19:53,830
Wow...

191
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:57,450
I want to be as globally renowned as her.

192
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:05,910
Huh?

193
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:07,170
What's up?

194
00:20:07,170 --> 00:20:09,660
- The DNA from these remains.
- Yeah?

195
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:13,130
We have a complete match to it
in our systems.

196
00:20:13,130 --> 00:20:14,850
A complete match?

197
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:18,770
Yeah. The gene sequence is registered to...

198
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:20,740
Huh?

199
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:23,040
This laboratory.

200
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:24,400
What?

201
00:20:25,170 --> 00:20:27,950
It's apparently sample number...

202
00:20:27,950 --> 00:20:30,620
"T548".

203
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:49,020
[Shiharu Nanase]

204
00:20:54,370 --> 00:20:56,150
Shiharu?

205
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:07,270
[log.1]

206
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:12,290
<i>Impossible.</i>

207
00:21:13,330 --> 00:21:14,260
<i>These bones...</i>

208
00:21:14,260 --> 00:21:16,660
[T548]

209
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:18,510
<i>They can't be.</i>

210
00:21:19,870 --> 00:21:21,390
[Shiharu]

211
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:29,010
<i>This was a sample I brought in</i>

212
00:21:29,010 --> 00:21:32,190
<i>for orientation.</i>

213
00:21:32,190 --> 00:21:35,870
<i>A piece of Shiharu's hair.</i>

214
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:39,560
<i>If the DNA sequence is a complete match,</i>

215
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:45,060
<i>then these bones from two centuries ago,
are Shiharu's.</i>

216
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:25,140
Professor?

217
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:11,010
<i>You have those, and I'll have these!</i>

218
00:23:16,690 --> 00:23:18,850
<i>I can make a boat.</i>

219
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:23,160
<i>Burn the mill!</i>

220
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:31,460
The humans seem like the real monsters here.

221
00:23:39,650 --> 00:23:43,650
He must not know why they fear him.

222
00:23:49,110 --> 00:23:52,040
To wonder why you've been born...

223
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:47,000
And there are no mistakes in these results?

224
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:50,460
Of course not. We were only double-checking.

225
00:24:51,230 --> 00:24:54,990
See? Look at that radiocarbon dating.

226
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,430
These are definitely over two centuries old.

227
00:24:59,770 --> 00:25:01,980
I see.

228
00:25:01,980 --> 00:25:04,220
What's got you so down, rich kid?

229
00:25:04,220 --> 00:25:07,480
Is Mr. Ishimizaki putting you to good work?

230
00:25:11,470 --> 00:25:13,490
You alright?

231
00:25:13,490 --> 00:25:16,710
Don't feel like research is your only option.

232
00:25:16,710 --> 00:25:18,650
You can get a job, unlike aimless ol' me.

233
00:25:18,650 --> 00:25:20,940
- Sorry, I have to go.
- Hey!

234
00:25:20,940 --> 00:25:23,040
Make sure you get some sleep, alright?

235
00:25:24,880 --> 00:25:28,210
<i>Please leave a message after the tone.</i>

236
00:25:29,210 --> 00:25:31,010
This is Nanase, speaking.

237
00:25:32,370 --> 00:25:35,610
Professor Ishimizaki, are you home?

238
00:25:36,430 --> 00:25:39,830
I have something to tell you. It's urgent.

239
00:25:39,830 --> 00:25:43,930
I'm heading over right now.

240
00:26:16,230 --> 00:26:20,000
Professor, this is Nanase.

241
00:26:20,990 --> 00:26:22,640
Sir, are you home?

242
00:26:41,220 --> 00:26:42,960
Hello?

243
00:26:46,590 --> 00:26:49,380
Professor Ishimizaki?

244
00:26:52,180 --> 00:26:53,980
I'm coming in.

245
00:26:59,730 --> 00:27:01,220
Professor Ishimizaki?

246
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:09,140
Professor?

247
00:27:35,590 --> 00:27:37,120
Sir?

248
00:27:44,590 --> 00:27:46,150
Hello?

249
00:27:57,120 --> 00:27:58,670
Professor Ishimizaki?

250
00:28:04,030 --> 00:28:06,620
[Incoming call: Nanase]

251
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:13,230
Sir?

252
00:28:22,710 --> 00:28:24,620
P-Professor...

253
00:28:25,580 --> 00:28:26,960
Professor.

254
00:28:27,500 --> 00:28:29,330
Professor Ishimizaki!

255
00:28:47,790 --> 00:28:49,180
Yes?

256
00:28:50,170 --> 00:28:51,950
Yes, this is he.

257
00:28:55,270 --> 00:28:56,720
What?

258
00:28:58,190 --> 00:29:00,000
Ishimizaki has been...

259
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:08,810
Did you visit
Professor Ishimizaki's home often?

260
00:29:08,810 --> 00:29:10,540
Yes.

261
00:29:10,540 --> 00:29:13,160
I visited for advice
on research and analysis.

262
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:19,840
What were you doing last night,
until the time the Professor was found?

263
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:23,490
I was analyzing a specimen,
at the Professor's request.

264
00:29:23,490 --> 00:29:25,400
Alone?

265
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:30,330
No. Until around 7PM,
I was accompanied by a junior of mine.

266
00:29:30,330 --> 00:29:32,760
So you were alone, from 7PM till morning.

267
00:29:32,760 --> 00:29:36,040
What are you trying to say?

268
00:29:37,770 --> 00:29:39,880
Are you accusing me?

269
00:29:42,370 --> 00:29:46,560
What sort of research do you do
with Professor Ishimizaki?

270
00:29:50,570 --> 00:29:57,510
We're researching how patterns in DNA
has an effect on the genome.

271
00:29:58,170 --> 00:29:59,750
Yes, come in.

272
00:30:00,770 --> 00:30:02,850
Mayuzumi, a minute?

273
00:30:03,490 --> 00:30:06,400
Sorry, we're almost done here.

274
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:35,650
You mentioned the Professor requested
you analyze a specimen for him?

275
00:30:35,650 --> 00:30:36,970
Yes.

276
00:30:37,670 --> 00:30:42,130
I was analyzing a skeleton
from a lake in the Himalayas.

277
00:30:42,130 --> 00:30:44,830
You said it dated 200 years back.

278
00:30:44,830 --> 00:30:47,360
What were the results of your analysis?

279
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:52,120
There was an error in my first pass.
I'll have to redo it.

280
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:53,780
I see.

281
00:30:53,780 --> 00:30:56,620
Were the remains something of importance?

282
00:30:57,150 --> 00:31:02,340
Yes, they would be to any researcher.

283
00:31:04,470 --> 00:31:08,180
Well, the skeleton has been stolen.

284
00:31:08,860 --> 00:31:10,350
What?

285
00:31:11,020 --> 00:31:15,280
We went to check the laboratory
as you testified,

286
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:18,280
but nothing was found in the lab.

287
00:31:18,280 --> 00:31:20,970
The associated DNA samples
have also vanished.

288
00:32:08,770 --> 00:32:13,060
Dealing with the pressure from Xin Ming Ah?

289
00:32:13,060 --> 00:32:16,310
Or with the death of your friend, Ishimizaki?

290
00:32:16,310 --> 00:32:17,440
Sir, please back off.

291
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:21,020
Is his death tied to your father's incident?

292
00:32:21,020 --> 00:32:22,980
Leave us.

293
00:32:22,980 --> 00:32:26,400
Xin Ming Ah is buying your stock.
They'll eventually hold the reigns.

294
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,310
I will call the police.

295
00:32:27,310 --> 00:32:30,200
Trying to rid yourself
of your father's bad legacy?

296
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:33,850
- Mr. Nanase, answer me!
- Back off!

297
00:32:37,620 --> 00:32:40,440
You must be Maehara.

298
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:42,650
Right-hand man to President Nanase.

299
00:32:42,650 --> 00:32:45,230
I hear he has you do the dirty work?

300
00:32:46,410 --> 00:32:49,430
Nichie Pharmaceuticals
has nothing to say to you.

301
00:32:50,270 --> 00:32:53,550
Your other employees
have already told me plenty.

302
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:57,520
They know nothing you could benefit from.

303
00:33:15,530 --> 00:33:18,390
Make way, police.

304
00:33:29,710 --> 00:33:32,640
When will they let us back in?

305
00:33:40,970 --> 00:33:44,840
You cannot think of anything?

306
00:33:53,010 --> 00:33:56,230
Even something small
you've noticed would help.

307
00:34:15,870 --> 00:34:17,070
Hirama!

308
00:34:17,070 --> 00:34:19,820
Hirama, sir.

309
00:34:19,820 --> 00:34:22,500
I've got a real scoop for you.

310
00:34:22,500 --> 00:34:25,750
If it's another celebrity scandal,
I don't need it.

311
00:34:25,750 --> 00:34:27,280
How about a corporate one?

312
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:29,770
- I've heard enough conspiracies.
- Oh, it's no conspiracy.

313
00:34:29,770 --> 00:34:31,900
This is my chance at redemption.

314
00:34:31,900 --> 00:34:35,990
So you've said time and time again.
What's changed?

315
00:34:35,990 --> 00:34:38,420
A corporate's misusing their capital
for illegal stunts,

316
00:34:38,420 --> 00:34:43,620
and now a murder might be involved.

317
00:34:44,730 --> 00:34:47,770
Come back to me after you have the evidence,

318
00:34:47,770 --> 00:34:51,000
and not just hearsay.

319
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:55,050
This one's nothing like the rest, Hirama.

320
00:34:57,490 --> 00:35:01,170
So you'll listen once I gather the evidence?

321
00:35:03,750 --> 00:35:06,790
If it's a good story,

322
00:35:06,790 --> 00:35:10,100
I'll treat you to sushi, girls, whatever.

323
00:35:10,100 --> 00:35:12,150
I've had enough of hostess bars.

324
00:35:12,150 --> 00:35:13,350
Especially the cheap ones.

325
00:35:13,350 --> 00:35:15,350
You think I'm still a cheapskate?

326
00:35:15,350 --> 00:35:16,990
I can afford better now.

327
00:35:16,990 --> 00:35:18,870
Then it's a promise.

328
00:35:18,870 --> 00:35:22,930
I'll bring you that riveting scoop.

329
00:35:24,930 --> 00:35:26,760
Hey!

330
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:28,970
The hell's his problem?

331
00:35:30,060 --> 00:35:33,210
Hirama, you have ties to Onodera?

332
00:35:33,210 --> 00:35:35,990
Yeah. He used to work under me.

333
00:35:35,990 --> 00:35:38,500
I don't hear great things about him.

334
00:35:38,500 --> 00:35:39,660
I'm not surprised.

335
00:35:39,660 --> 00:35:43,580
Can you believe he used to be an earnest guy?

336
00:35:43,580 --> 00:35:46,420
He'd always work hard
to accomplish his goals.

337
00:35:46,420 --> 00:35:49,880
Always pushing me to do better.

338
00:35:49,880 --> 00:35:53,870
Seriously? That chronic blackmailer?

339
00:35:53,870 --> 00:35:58,040
Yeah. I guess serious guys
tend to break heart early.

340
00:35:58,040 --> 00:36:00,370
Not me, though.

341
00:36:01,380 --> 00:36:02,620
Yeah, yeah.

342
00:36:02,620 --> 00:36:06,450
While we were questioning Haruka Nanase,

343
00:36:06,450 --> 00:36:10,430
the sample he was analyzing
at the Professor's request, vanished.

344
00:36:10,430 --> 00:36:12,530
The culprit is likely the very same.

345
00:36:12,530 --> 00:36:17,330
The university's security tapes
have already been overwritten.

346
00:36:17,330 --> 00:36:20,930
There's nothing incriminating on them.

347
00:36:23,440 --> 00:36:27,480
[Funeral, Akihiko Ishimizaki]

348
00:36:47,150 --> 00:36:52,130
<i>The world you see now,
is not the whole truth.</i>

349
00:37:06,290 --> 00:37:08,300
Dr. Senba has arrived.

350
00:37:44,210 --> 00:37:47,400
I think all relevant data has been wiped.

351
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:50,720
Including the university security tapes?

352
00:37:50,720 --> 00:37:53,940
Yes.

353
00:37:53,940 --> 00:37:58,420
Though the cameras automatically reset
every 30 days,

354
00:37:58,420 --> 00:38:01,670
this incident occurred
on the 17th day in that cycle.

355
00:38:01,670 --> 00:38:03,770
How thorough.

356
00:38:03,770 --> 00:38:06,110
Something's definitely up.

357
00:38:06,110 --> 00:38:09,200
I'm betting on foul play.

358
00:38:19,310 --> 00:38:21,020
Are you okay?

359
00:38:22,020 --> 00:38:24,120
I'll drive you home.

360
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:26,210
It's fine. I'd rather walk.

361
00:38:29,530 --> 00:38:31,190
What happened?

362
00:38:33,820 --> 00:38:35,940
Talk to me.

363
00:38:35,940 --> 00:38:38,350
I promise I won't doubt you.

364
00:38:43,330 --> 00:38:45,720
Have you heard of Roopkund?

365
00:38:49,450 --> 00:38:52,090
I believe so.

366
00:38:52,090 --> 00:38:55,150
It's a lake, located in the Himalayas.

367
00:38:55,740 --> 00:38:58,660
Professor Ishimizaki requested that I...

368
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:03,410
That I analyze one of the skeletons

369
00:39:03,960 --> 00:39:08,570
found by the lake.

370
00:39:08,570 --> 00:39:12,400
Ishimizaki asked you to do an analysis?

371
00:39:12,400 --> 00:39:13,840
Yes.

372
00:39:14,660 --> 00:39:17,000
Professor Ishimizaki passed away

373
00:39:17,700 --> 00:39:20,000
before I could report

374
00:39:21,170 --> 00:39:23,810
my findings to him.

375
00:39:24,950 --> 00:39:27,260
Alright, take it easy.

376
00:39:31,520 --> 00:39:33,010
Sit.

377
00:39:39,700 --> 00:39:41,750
Breathe in, slowly.

378
00:39:43,610 --> 00:39:45,180
Steady yourself.

379
00:39:46,150 --> 00:39:47,600
Right.

380
00:39:50,030 --> 00:39:54,880
So you analyzed these bones.

381
00:39:56,950 --> 00:39:58,340
Yes.

382
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:02,430
According to my findings,

383
00:40:04,950 --> 00:40:07,120
the DNA sequence of these remains

384
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:14,390
were a perfect match to Shiharu's sample.

385
00:40:23,550 --> 00:40:25,600
It's true.

386
00:40:31,690 --> 00:40:33,590
I believe you.

387
00:40:35,870 --> 00:40:37,400
Really?

388
00:40:41,730 --> 00:40:44,160
Can we talk more about this, alone?

389
00:40:44,790 --> 00:40:46,710
I want to hear more.

390
00:40:46,710 --> 00:40:49,620
Can you make time for me?

391
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:55,420
- Yes.
- Until then, keep it our secret.

392
00:40:55,940 --> 00:40:59,000
We wouldn't want to accidentally
tarnish Ishimizaki's name, right?

393
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:01,210
Right.

394
00:41:03,710 --> 00:41:07,630
Breathe in, slowly.

395
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:16,090
How about you visit the clinic?
I'll drive you there.

396
00:41:19,890 --> 00:41:21,510
You don't believe me after all.

397
00:41:21,510 --> 00:41:23,060
No, I'm just worried about you.

398
00:41:23,060 --> 00:41:25,000
I don't believe it either.

399
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:29,840
For now, you're better off
keeping your findings to yourself.

400
00:41:32,630 --> 00:41:35,740
"Don't raise a fuss about this", is that it?

401
00:41:35,740 --> 00:41:37,670
You made yourself clear enough.

402
00:41:37,670 --> 00:41:39,460
No, that's not it.

403
00:41:39,460 --> 00:41:41,980
Haruka, there's something
you still don't know.

404
00:41:44,070 --> 00:41:47,960
But this isn't the place to talk about it.

405
00:41:53,570 --> 00:41:56,030
I see you're without a hammer today.

406
00:41:58,480 --> 00:42:01,020
You are Haruka Nanase, yes?

407
00:42:02,250 --> 00:42:06,690
I am Ishimizaki's niece, Yui.

408
00:42:08,670 --> 00:42:11,980
- Oh, my...
- I am not here to ask for condolences.

409
00:42:13,870 --> 00:42:19,010
I wish to ask about my uncle's death.

410
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:23,850
Shall we walk a bit?

411
00:42:30,790 --> 00:42:34,860
You are my uncle's assistant, correct?

412
00:42:34,860 --> 00:42:36,670
Yes.

413
00:42:36,670 --> 00:42:39,960
Why did you go to my uncle's house that day?

414
00:42:42,670 --> 00:42:47,460
You may be able to deceive the police,
but not me.

415
00:42:51,670 --> 00:42:54,370
I know you're hiding something.

416
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:06,010
Wait.

417
00:43:06,630 --> 00:43:09,450
Please, listen to what I have to say.

418
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:14,040
Mari is gone.

419
00:43:16,120 --> 00:43:21,060
She went missing after my uncle's death.

420
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:27,070
Mari... Ishimizaki's daughter?

421
00:43:27,070 --> 00:43:28,920
- Yes.
- In the wheelchair?

422
00:43:28,920 --> 00:43:30,410
Yes.

423
00:43:30,410 --> 00:43:32,930
She has disappeared.

424
00:43:32,930 --> 00:43:36,180
- Does the police know?
- Of course.

425
00:43:36,710 --> 00:43:37,980
Then they'll handle it.

426
00:43:37,980 --> 00:43:41,770
Did you leave things to the police as well?

427
00:43:44,850 --> 00:43:49,420
Were you calm when your sister disappeared?

428
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:04,320
Please.

429
00:44:05,410 --> 00:44:09,880
If there's anything you know,
won't you share it with me?

430
00:44:12,940 --> 00:44:15,200
What do you know?

431
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:21,220
Nothing, yet.

432
00:44:22,630 --> 00:44:27,440
But I am one of the few people
who knew my uncle well.

433
00:44:27,440 --> 00:44:31,390
Why don't we work together,
for the sake of our own goals?

434
00:44:31,950 --> 00:44:33,910
Work together?

435
00:44:33,910 --> 00:44:35,710
Yes.

436
00:44:35,710 --> 00:44:41,340
"Cooperation is the key to humans surviving
a multitude of scenarios".

437
00:44:42,510 --> 00:44:46,780
It's a quote from Nichola Raihani,
an evolutionary biologist.

438
00:44:54,420 --> 00:44:56,180
Sorry.

439
00:44:58,310 --> 00:45:00,960
I just wanted to seem a bit smart.

440
00:45:05,260 --> 00:45:07,850
<i>I just wanted to seem a bit smart.</i>

441
00:45:21,410 --> 00:45:24,560
We're still unsure.

442
00:45:24,560 --> 00:45:28,550
We've got the body, but no identity.

443
00:45:45,490 --> 00:45:46,820
A monster?

444
00:45:46,820 --> 00:45:49,630
We have no other leads!

445
00:45:50,170 --> 00:45:53,040
We've only got the bones.

446
00:45:53,040 --> 00:45:55,640
No decomposed matter in sight.
